{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's same-trip burden under POL-RD-08(a) is met on the face of the bundle: EV-TRIP-00108, EV-GPS-00108 and EV-FARE-00108 all carry trip_id TRP-00108, and the trace runs from the 07:19:20 start to the 07:53:20 end recorded on the trip record, so the artifacts plainly describe one and the same trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-GPS-00108", "EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On this trip's own measurements the deviation is established. The governing figure under POL-RD-01 is gps_trace.trace_distance_km, 26.17 km, and the platform's own pre-pass records the resulting excess as 5.17 km, or 24.6% of the 21.0 km booked optimal, which clears both POL-RD-01 thresholds (greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms and greater than 20% of optimal). The rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 26.2 km is a convenience copy of the same measurement and must not be substituted for the trace figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Once that excess is shown, POL-RD-08 shifts the burden to the driver to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause, and no extra corroboration is demanded of this rider: the rider-profile condition that would require corroboration beyond the gps_trace bites only where rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more, and on EV-RPROF-00108 that field is 1, so the rider is exactly the low-frequency claimant the proviso does not touch.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's two chat messages cannot be turned into a rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04. That clause requires the requested waypoint to be taken from chat_message.waypoint_hint, and every message on EV-CHAT-00108 carries waypoint_hint null with no road named, so the corroboration test is undecidable on the record, the clause is unavailable, and the case must be decided on the remaining clauses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no road-closure answer to this claim either. The only traffic-advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00108-01, is a MISSING artifact that keeps its identifier, carries no payload and holds weight 0.0 under a MISSING_ARTIFACT issue; no advisory therefore names any road, expressway segment or junction the optimal route traverses, and POL-RD-03 can exonerate nothing. The rider cites the absence itself.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00108-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's answer is POL-RD-05, but that clause re-bases the optimal; it does not wipe the slate for his own driving. Even on the amended re-quote the platform stored, 24.60 km, the driver's own trace of 26.17 km exceeds the amended optimal by 1.57 km, and the trace records two loops of the T3 departure kerb well inside 380 m of the amended pin - the very circling the rider complains of and the driver concedes ('I went round the loop twice'). The POL-RD-05 circling exclusion does not shelter that distance: it applies only where the rider was not at the amended point, and on the rider's account she was waiting at T3.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00108", "EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-CHAT-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money then follows arithmetically, not discretionarily, under POL-RD-02 on this METERED fare, and EV-FARE-00108 already carries the platform's own computation against the booked optimal: charged_total 33.77, recomputed_fare 27.63, and a refund of 6.15. That is above the 0.50 de-minimis floor and below the 90% full-refund share, so the rider's remedy is the PARTIAL_REFUND the clause provides, stated on the ruling's separate lines of charged_total, recomputed_fare and refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the Tribunal cannot reconcile, within the record alone, the pre-pass reading of the optimal at 21.0 km with the amended re-quote of 24.60 km that POL-RD-05 directs it to use, then the case is not safely resolvable at the POL-RD-10 confidence floor of 0.70 and the correct outcome is ESCALATE, under which the disputed sum is held rather than collected - not NO_ACTION, which on a rider-filed dispute leaves the charge standing against her.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00108", "EV-GPS-00108", "EV-FARE-00108"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-05", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: This began as a Rivervale Drive to Changi T1 booking, but it ended as a Punggol MRT to Changi T3 trip. The rider moved the pickup pin to Punggol MRT at 07:12 (chat MSG-00108-001, acknowledged by the driver at 07:12:15) and changed the drop to T3 at 07:41 (MSG-00108-003, acknowledged at 07:42:05). Under POL-RD-05, where an endpoint has been amended after booking, the route must be re-measured against the platform's own post-amendment re-quote - here amended_optimal_distance_km 24.60 km with amended_optimal_duration_min 31.0 - and not against the 21.0 km booked Rivervale-to-T1 figure. Measured properly, the governing actual distance is the GPS trace figure of 26.17 km, and the excess over the amended optimal is 26.17 minus 24.60 = 1.57 km, about 6.4% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires both limbs to pass - more than 0.8 km absolute and more than 20% of optimal - and 6.4% fails the percentage limb. No deviation is established, and POL-RD-05 states the outcome in terms: NO_ACTION. The rider's claim that the deviation is 'established' at 5.17 km / 24.6% (excess_pct) is rejected: that figure was derived against the superseded 21.0 km booked optimal, and POL-RD-01 requires establishment to be assessed on the excess remaining after the POL-RD-05 adjustment. The rider's profile point that deviation_claims_60d is only 1 (so no extra corroboration is demanded) is accepted but is moot, because the threshold itself is not met. On the 'five minutes driving around the airport': that is the T3 kerb loop, and POL-RD-05 excludes circling within 400 m of an amended pin; even counting it, the whole-trip excess stays far under the 20% limb, so it cannot establish a deviation in either direction. The rider's fallback arguments do not change this. POL-RD-04 (rider-requested detour) is correctly unavailable: every chat message carries waypoint_hint null, so the corroboration test cannot be run, exactly as the clause provides. POL-RD-03 is unavailable because EV-ADVIS-00108-01 is a MISSING artifact at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and no advisory names any road - but there is no surviving excess for it to exonerate. The escalation argument is rejected: the record reconciles within itself, because POL-RD-05 expressly directs use of the stored amended re-quote of 24.60 km, which is present and non-null, so the 0.70 confidence floor is not approached and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. On the money lines: the airport_surcharge is correctly 0.00 because this trip ENDS at Changi rather than originating there, and erp_gantries and tolls are 0.00, so there is no billing-integrity correction under POL-RD-09(4) and no referral. No repeat-deviation pattern exists under POL-RD-06 (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 402), so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (206 fixes, 10 s interval, 100% coverage, max gap 0.0 s), so no independent corroboration is required and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation applies. Result: the rider's claim is not supported on the corrected measurement. The present state stands - payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 are left as they are, and the $33.77 charge remains in place; no refund is ordered. Deciding figures used: 26.17 km trace distance, 24.60 km amended optimal, 1.57 km and 6.4% excess, against the superseded 21.0 km / 5.17 km / 24.6% booked-route comparison, and charged_total $33.77.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Rider and Driver, this ruling is NO_ACTION. The $33.77 charge stands and no refund or compensation is ordered.\n\nThe reason is the route-deviation threshold. The trip record shows that both endpoints were amended after booking: the rider moved the pickup to Punggol MRT at 07:12:30, and the rider changed the dropoff to Changi T3 at 07:41:52. POL-RD-05 therefore requires the optimal-route baseline to be the platform's post-amendment re-quote, which is 24.60 km (amended_optimal_distance_km), not the original 21.0 km booked optimal. The GPS trace is complete and unimpaired (206 fixes, 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps). Its trace distance is 26.17 km. The excess over the amended optimal is 26.17 - 24.60 = 1.57 km, which is 6.4% of 24.60. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be both greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20% of the optimal. The absolute test passes, but the percentage test fails, so no deviation is established.\n\nThe rider's argument that the deviation is established against the 21.0 km booked optimal is rejected: POL-RD-05 displaces the booked optimal once an endpoint is amended, and the pre-pass 'established' flag on the GPS artifact was computed against the booked figure. The rider's argument that a $6.15 refund is due under POL-RD-02 is rejected because POL-RD-02 only runs once a deviation is established. The rider's alternative request for escalation under POL-RD-10 is also rejected: the record is reconcilable by applying POL-RD-05, so there is no unresolved conflict. For completeness, the fare breakdown records charged_total 33.77, a platform recomputed_fare of 27.63 and a notional refund of 6.15 against the booked 21.0 km optimal; because no deviation is established after the POL-RD-05 re-basing, those figures are not ordered.\n\nThe driver's POL-RD-05 argument is accepted. The driver's argument that the T3 kerb circling should be excluded does not need to be resolved: even if the circling distance were included, the excess is only 1.57 km and fails the 20% limb. The rider's contrary account of being at the kerb is therefore not determinative.\n\nOn the other points: POL-RD-04 is unavailable because the chat messages carry waypoint_hint null and name no road, so no rider-requested detour can be established; POL-RD-03 cannot exonerate because the only traffic advisory is missing (weight 0.0). The fare breakdown shows no billing-integrity defect: the airport surcharge is 0.00 and correctly so for a trip ending at Changi, and there are no ERP gantries. POL-RD-06 does not fire because driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 402 completed trips in 90 days, so no FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral. POL-RD-07 is satisfied: the trace is not impaired under limbs (a)-(c), so no POL-RD-10(3) escalation. The rider's profile shows deviation_claims_60d of 1, so the POL-RD-08 corroboration proviso does not apply, but that point is academic because no deviation survives the threshold.\n\nConfidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. No referrals are issued. The disputed amount remains charged according to the present state."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
